>
  <p>An <strong>online calorie calculator</strong> is the fastest way to find your daily calorie needs. It runs in any web browser, works on phones and computers alike, and gives you personalized numbers instantly — all free and without creating an account.</p>

  <h2>Why use an online calorie calculator instead of an app?</h2>
  <p>Online calculators have advantages over apps: no download required, no storage space taken, and no need to create an account. They also update automatically — no app store visits needed. Our calculator works offline-ready and saves your recent inputs on your device.</p>

  <h2>How the online calorie calculator works</h2>
  <p>The calculator uses your age, sex, height, weight, and activity level to compute your BMR (Basal Metabolic Rate) with the Mifflin-St Jeor equation. It then multiplies by an activity factor to get your TDEE (Total Daily Energy Expenditure) — your maintenance calories. Finally, it adjusts for your goal: deficit for weight loss, surplus for gain.</p>

  <h2>Benefits of our online calorie calculator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No signup or download</strong> — use it immediately in your browser.</li>
    <li><strong>Mobile optimized</strong> — works on any device with a fast, app-like experience.</li>
    <li><strong>Complete results</strong> — shows calories, macros, and weekly weight targets.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy first</strong> — calculations run in your browser, data never leaves your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Free forever</strong> — no paywalls, no limits, no hidden costs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How accurate is an online calorie calculator?</h2>
  <p>An online calorie calculator using Mifflin-St Jeor is the most accurate accessible formula, with research showing it's typically within 10–15% of measured values. No calculator can predict individual metabolism perfectly, so track your results for 2–3 weeks and adjust as needed.</p>

  <h2>Why search for 'online calorie calculator'?</h2>
  <p>People search for online calorie calculators when they want immediate, private answers to "how many calories should I eat?" The online format provides convenience, no-commitment access, and instant results that help you make informed food choices.</p>

  <h2>How to use an online calorie calculator for weight loss</h2>
  <p>Enter your stats, choose a weight-loss goal, and the online calculator gives you a daily calorie target below your maintenance. Eat at or near this target consistently. For more guidance, read our <a href="/guides/weight-loss-guide/">weight loss guide</a>.</p>
